# Option 1 — Actions live in the card header

No standalone header row. Add-button + archived toggle merge into the existing
Card title row. Old description becomes an (i) tooltip on the title.

```
┌─ Card ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Labels (4) (i)             Show archived (2)      [ + New label ]│
├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ (● Urgent)                                                    ✎  │
│ (● Backlog)                                                   ✎  │
│ (● Blocked)                                                   ✎  │
│ (● Waiting)                                                   ✎  │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

hover (i):
        ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────┐
        │ Shared vocabulary — apply to a concept or to │
        │ individual items. Managing is admin-only.    │
        └──────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

Views (stacked sortable cards) gets a slim header strip instead, same idea:

```
┌─ Views (3) (i) ─────────────────────────────────[ + New view ]──┐
│ ⠿ Default                          org                       ✎  │
│ ⠿ My focus                         personal                  ✎  │
│ ⠿ Roadmap                          org                       ✎  │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

+ zero vertical waste; everything in one box
+ CardHeader already has `action` slot — small change
- archived list still needs its own card below (unchanged)
